<http://data.silknow.org/object/fbcf874b-7cd8-3382-9c10-fc8ec95a8f01/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This chair is from a set of seat furniture orginally at Glenham Hall, in Suffolk. Glenham Hall was the seat of the North family. The set of furniture, which comprises ten chairs, two stools, and two settees, dates from the 1720s. It may have been made in 1722, when alterations were carried out Glenham Hall. The set is remarkable for its rich carving and original gilding. \n\nThe stool is currently on loan to Marble Hill House."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/fbcf874b-7cd8-3382-9c10-fc8ec95a8f01> .

